{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>The Festival of Unleavened Bread you shall keep.</b> After prohibiting the molten image, whose makers intended to attain only transient life, He mentioned commandments through which are drawn kinds of imagined successes such as spring, harvest, ingathering, and the pursuits of acquisitions, and He arranged them in this passage according to the order in which they were given to Israel. The first of them is the Festival of Unleavened Bread <b>at the appointed season of the month of the spring</b>, through which the spring is blessed. Second, the matter of the firstborn, through which livestock are blessed — this being the commandment given immediately after the Festival of Unleavened Bread at their departure from Egypt. Third, the commandment of the Sabbath, which was given at Marah, through which the days of work are blessed, as it says: שֵׁשֶׁת יָמִים תַּעֲשֶׂה מַעֲשֶׂיךָ (Exodus 23:12), and together with it He spoke of the seventh year, which blesses the years, as it says: שֵׁשׁ שָׁנִים תִּזְרַע (Exodus 23:10). Fourth, the Festival of Harvest, which is Shavuot — חֻקּוֹת קָצִיר יִשְׁמָר לָנוּ (Jeremiah 5:24). Fifth, the Festival of Ingathering, through which the ingathering is blessed, as it says: כְּבִרְכַּת ה' אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲשֶׁר נָתַן לָךְ (Deuteronomy 16:16). And after these commandments He mentioned a comprehensive commandment for all three pilgrimage festivals, namely יֵרָאֶה כָּל זְכוּרְךָ, and after that He mentioned commandments specific to the Festival of Unleavened Bread: לֹא תִשְׁחַט עַל חָמֵץ and לֹא יָלִין, and after that He mentioned a commandment specific to the majority for the Festival of Harvest, namely רֵאשִׁית בִּכּוּרֵי אַדְמָתְךָ, as they said, of blessed memory: מֵעֲצֶרֶת וְעַד הֶחָג מֵבִיא וְקוֹרֵא (Mishnah Bikkurim 1:6), and after that He mentioned a commandment specific to the majority for the Festival of Sukkot, namely לֹא תְבַשֵּׁל גְּדִי, for that is the season of kids, as some of them said, of blessed memory: בְּאֶחָד בְּתִשְׁרֵי רֹאשׁ הַשָּׁנָה לְמַעְשַׂר בְּהֵמָה (Mishnah Rosh HaShanah 2:1)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "Where Sforno writes 'the molten image' (אֱלֹהֵי מַסֵּכָה), he refers to the golden calf prohibition immediately preceding in 34:17; rendered literally to preserve his reference."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:28:14.944806575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}